  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Small businesses obligated $23.4B in federal contract dollars in FY2026 to date. ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. leads the list with $3.3B in obligations. CSI AVIATION, INC obligated $1.1B, W S DARLEY & CO obligated $1B, and AMERICAN CENTRIFUGE OPERATING, LLC obligated $916M. GENERAL MATTER, INC. obligated $900M, MINBURN TECHNOLOGY GROUP, LLC obligated $801M, THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC obligated $799M, FOUR POINTS TECHNOLOGY, L.L.C. obligated $743M, V3GATE, LLC obligated $738M, and COCHRANE USA INC obligated $641M round out the top ten. All figures are contract obligations. The FY2026 totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. Procurement officers and small-business leaders can use the ranking to see which vendors captured the largest obligation totals so far in the fiscal year. The list highlights concentration at the top where a handful of small businesses account for multi-hundred-million and multi-billion obligation totals within the current fiscal period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who occupies the top of the ranking?",
        "body": "ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC. occupies the top position with $3.3B in obligations. CSI AVIATION, INC is second with $1.1B and W S DARLEY & CO is third with $1B. The remaining top ten obligations range from $916M down to $641M, showing several firms with high single-company totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What limitations should readers keep in mind about these figures?",
        "body": "All figures are contract obligations, and the FY2026 totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. The ranking lists absolute obligation totals; it does not reflect contract counts, award types, or future performance. Readers should treat these numbers as a snapshot of obligations within the current fiscal period."
      }
    ]
  },
